    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36458" root="قيس" body-key="q">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قِيَاسٌ</span></b> : see 1 and 3. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [Used as a simple
subst., <i>Measurement.</i> ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <i>Comparison.</i> ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  <i>Ratiocination.</i> ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b5-  The <i>premises of a syllogism, taken together:</i> and also applied to <i>a syllogism</i> entire. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b6- 
<i>Analogy: rule.</i> You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هٰذَا عَلَى القِيَاسِ</span> <i>This
is according to analogy,</i> or <i>to rule.</i> And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هٰذَا</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَلَى غَيْرِ قيَاسٍ</span> <i>This is contrary to analogy,</i> or <i>to
rule.</i> And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَلَى قِيَاسِ كَذَا</span> <i>After the manner of
such a thing.</i>]

